**### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):**  

The screening was performed automatically using the following logic:

| Decision rule | Description |
|---|---|
| **Randomisation** | The abstract or title must contain “randomized”, “randomised”, “RCT”, “randomised controlled 
trial”, or “randomized controlled trial”. |
| **Population** | Must refer to adults (≥ 18 y) with heart‑failure (HF). This was inferred from the presence of “heart 
failure”, “HF”, or similar terms. |
| **Intervention** | Must be an mHealth‑delivered *education* programme (not just monitoring). Keywords used: `app`, 
`smartphone`, `tablet`, `mobile`, `web`, `internet`, `online`, `e‑health`, `mHealth`, `SMS`, `text message`, `social 
media`, `video education`, `website`, `digital`, `remote education`. |
| **Comparator** | Must be “usual care” (any mention of usual HF care, standard care, control group receiving routine 
care). |
| **Study design** | Must be a Randomised Controlled Trial (RCT). |

If **all** conditions were satisfied, the study was marked **INCLUDE**; otherwise **EXCLUDE**.  The rule is deliberately
conservative – any uncertainty leads to exclusion because the intervention must be *education* delivered via a mobile or
web platform.

