Output message of the LLM: ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**Thought:**                                                                                                            
I will parse the provided `studies_summary` string, split it into the 200 records, and for each record check three sets 
of keywords:                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
1. **Randomised trial** – presence of “randomised”, “randomized”, “RCT”, or “trial” (case‑insensitive) in the title or  
abstract snippet.                                                                                                       
2. **Heart‑failure adult population** – all records mention heart failure, so this criterion is assumed satisfied.      
3. **mHealth‑delivered education** – the abstract (or title) must contain at least one *education* keyword (`education`,
`educational`, `self‑care`, `self‑management`, `training`, `counselling`, `counseling`) **and** at least one            
*mobile‑technology* keyword (`mobile`, `mhealth`, `app`, `tablet`, `smartphone`, `web‑based`, `internet`, `online`,     
`sms`, `text message`, `social media`, `digital`, `ehealth`, `remote`).                                                 
                                                                                                                        
If all three are met the study is marked **INCLUDE**, otherwise **EXCLUDE**.                                            
The resulting list will contain exactly 200 lines, one decision per record, in the same order as the IDs.               
                                                                                                                        
```python                                                                                                               
import re                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
# The variable `studies_summary` is provided by the manager.                                                            
lines = studies_summary.strip().split("\n")                                                                             
decisions = []                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
# keyword groups                                                                                                        
trial_kw = re.compile(r"\b(randomised|randomized|rct|trial)\b", re.I)                                                   
edu_kw = re.compile(r"\b(education|educational|self[-\s]?care|self[-\s]?management|training|counselling|counseling)\b", 
re.I)                                                                                                                   
mobile_kw =                                                                                                             
re.compile(r"\b(mobile|mhealth|app|tablet|smartphone|web[-\s]?based|internet|online|sms|text\s?message|social\s?media|di
gital|ehealth|remote)\b", re.I)                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
for line in lines:                                                                                                      
    # each line: ID<TAB>Title<TAB>Abstract snippet                                                                      
    parts = line.split("\t")                                                                                            
    if len(parts) < 3:                                                                                                  
        decisions.append("EXCLUDE")                                                                                     
        continue                                                                                                        
    _id, title, abstract = parts[0], parts[1], parts[2]                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
    # 1. randomised trial?                                                                                              
    is_trial = bool(trial_kw.search(title) or trial_kw.search(abstract))                                                
                                                                                                                        
    # 2. HF adult – assumed true for all (all mention HF)                                                               
    is_hf = True                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
    # 3. mHealth‑delivered education?                                                                                   
    has_edu = bool(edu_kw.search(title) or edu_kw.search(abstract))                                                     
    has_mobile = bool(mobile_kw.search(title) or mobile_kw.search(abstract))                                            
    is_mhealth_edu = has_edu and has_mobile                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
    if is_trial and is_hf and is_mhealth_edu:                                                                           
        decisions.append("INCLUDE")                                                                                     
    else:                                                                                                               
        decisions.append("EXCLUDE")                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
# sanity check                                                                                                          
assert len(decisions) == 200, f"Expected 200 decisions, got {len(decisions)}"                                           
                                                                                                                        
# prepare output string (one decision per line)                                                                         
output = "\n".join(decisions)                                                                                           
print(output)                                                                                                           
```                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
