━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ Step 4 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
Output message of the LLM: ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**Thought:**                                                                                                            
I will parse the provided `titles_summary` (each line: ID<TAB>Title) and apply simple heuristics to decide inclusion:   
                                                                                                                        
1. **RCT requirement:** Title must contain words like “randomized”, “randomised”, “randomised controlled trial”, “RCT”, 
“randomized trial”, “pilot study” (often RCT), or “randomized clinical trial”.                                          
2. **Adult HF population:** Titles mentioning “heart failure”, “HF”, or “congestive heart failure” are assumed to       
involve adults (≥ 18 y) unless explicitly pediatric.                                                                    
3. **mHealth‑delivered education:** Title must contain at least one mobile‑health term (`mobile`, `smartphone`,         
`tablet`, `app`, `web`, `internet`, `online`, `SMS`, `text`, `e‑health`, `m‑health`, `digital`, `social media`,         
`phone‑based`, `remote`, `telemonitoring` when paired with “education”, “self‑management”, “counseling”, “training”,    
“knowledge”, “patient‑centered”, etc.).                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
If a title satisfies both (1) and (3) together with an HF context, I will mark it **INCLUDE**; otherwise **EXCLUDE**.   
The heuristic is deliberately conservative – if the title contains the required elements but the exact nature of the    
intervention is unclear, I will still include it (it can be excluded later).                                            
                                                                                                                        
**Code:**                                                                                                               
The code extracts each line, applies the heuristics, prints the decision list (200 lines), and finally returns it via   
`final_answer`.                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
```python                                                                                                               
titles = titles_summary.splitlines()                                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
import re                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
def decide(title):                                                                                                      
    # lower‑case for easier matching                                                                                    
    t = title.lower()                                                                                                   
    # RCT indicator                                                                                                     
    rct = bool(re.search(r'\brandomi[sz]ed\b|\brandomised\b|\brct\b|\brandomized controlled trial\b|\brandomised        
controlled trial\b|\bpilot study\b|\bclinical trial\b', t))                                                             
    # HF population indicator                                                                                           
    hf = bool(re.search(r'heart failure|hf|congestive heart failure', t))                                               
    # mHealth education indicator                                                                                       
    mobile_terms = r'mobile|smartphone|tablet|app|web|internet|online|sms|text|e[- ]?health|m[- ]?health|digital|social 
media|phone[- ]?based|telemonitoring|remote'                                                                            
    education_terms = r'education|educational|self[- ]?management|counseling|training|knowledge|patient[-               
]?centered|self[- ]?care|behavio?ur|learning|support|programme|program|intervention'                                    
    mhealth = bool(re.search(mobile_terms, t)) and bool(re.search(education_terms, t))                                  
    return "INCLUDE" if rct and hf and mhealth else "EXCLUDE"                                                           
                                                                                                                        
decisions = [decide(line.split('\t',1)[1]) for line in titles]                                                          
                                                                                                                        
# Ensure we have exactly 200 decisions (one per ID)                                                                     
assert len(decisions) == 200, f"Expected 200 decisions, got {len(decisions)}"                                           
                                                                                                                        
# Output each decision on its own line                                                                                  
output = "\n".join(decisions)                                                                                           
print(output)                                                                                                           
```                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                        
