### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                                
- **Inclusion logic:** A study was marked **INCLUDE** only when the abstract (or title) explicitly mentioned a          
**randomised controlled trial** (or “randomised”, “randomised controlled”), **adults with heart failure**, and an       
**mHealth‑delivered educational component** (e.g., tablet/computer/Internet/web‑based program, smartphone/app, SMS, or  
other mobile‑device education).                                                                                         
- **Exclusion logic:** Studies lacking any of the three pillars above (randomisation, HF population, mHealth education) 
were excluded. Protocols, reviews, feasibility pilots without randomisation, and interventions centred solely on        
telemonitoring, medication reminders, or disease‑management without an explicit education‑delivery mechanism were also  
excluded.                                                                                                               
- **Confidence:** All decisions are given **high confidence** because they are based on clear textual cues in the       
provided titles/abstracts; no inference beyond the supplied information was required.                                   
